    "body": "pulse task #2644 \u00b7 generation 1.\n\n<!-- pulse-operation:3d835823e461566d38460080f5c528dd -->\n\nassigned to @PORTALSURFER. the frozen task plan is retained in pulse and copied below.\n\n# Pulse task #2644: Support computer keyboard monitoring with positive-latency signal graphs\n\nOperation: 3d835823e461566d38460080f5c528dd\nAssignee: PORTALSURFER (Pulse #1, GitHub ID 41680373)\n\nFollow-up from computer MIDI keyboard #2642 / https://github.com/PORTALSURFER/hex/pull/257. Initial implementation explicitly refuses live bank preparation when the prepared signal graph has positive compensation or device latency; zero-latency routing remains supported.\n\nReason: advancing existing compensation rings with frozen musical clocks while stopped can drain pre-pause authored samples and overwrite delay history, changing resume behavior. Do not silently reset/cut authored delay state to enable audition.\n\nAcceptance: define isolated live-monitor delay ownership or another explicit architecture preserving pause/resume history, existing authored routes and physical input release/Stop semantics; bound combined graph/storage/work and retirement; test positive track/device latency, stopped/live routing, mixed authored/live playback, pause/resume PCM continuity, stale publication, rollback and callback zero allocations/deallocations. Keep offline/export unaffected. This is deferred implementation, not a blocker for the bounded zero-latency keyboard feature.\n\ncreated by pulse shared PR intake/start task. builds, checks and merging follow the repository's own instructions.",
